{"type":"message","id":"0717c1a4","parentId":"139e5205","timestamp":"2026-05-20T13:03:21.402Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Still unauthorized for POST. The GET requests work with `X-API-Key` but POST doesn't. Maybe the POST endpoint requires different authentication. Let me try with `GET` first to see if there's a different format for POST auth.\n\nActually, wait - looking more carefully at the initial results, the GET requests succeeded with `X-API-Key`, but now they're failing. That's odd. Let me recheck...\n\nOh wait, looking back: the first GET (with Bearer) returned \"Unauthorized\", then I switched to `X-API-Key` and both GETs returned data successfully. But now even the `X-API-Key` header isn't working for POST. Maybe I need to try different content types or different JSON field formats.\n\n\nLet me just test the POST endpoint with various combinations to see what actually works. The GET worked fine so the API key itself seems valid, but POST might have different requirements - possibly needing a different header format, different body structure, or even a different endpoint path altogether.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-eaca1a0b-9563-46f5-9ff8-5ae693e1df6e","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try POST with different formats\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"message\":\"heartbeat test 13:00 UTC\",\"type\":\"message\"}'"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-32ed450a-f15c-44f9-b78b-3dac326999bb","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Check what methods/paths are available\ncurl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":6789,"output":355,"cacheRead":11